READING THIS
------------
handoff 2026-08-21 sec.4 pre-registered three outcomes, and the per-stream
table above is what picks between them:

  the CO2 seasonal rows veto it   -> the air-sea flux response is too STRONG;
      suspect the solubility-only formulation (no seasonal MLD, no biology)
      applied to a single hemispheric box
  the d13C seasonal rows veto it  -> the PARTITION is wrong, not the amplitude.
      The ocean channel is isotopically near-neutral (0.0045), so adding it
      should HELP the signature -- a d13C veto is genuinely surprising and is
      a place to STOP and think rather than push on
  the annual/level rows veto it   -> the seasonal term is LEAKING into the
      annual budget, which is a BUG: it is zero-annual-mean by construction

Only if this is inconclusive is a new observational product worth it (a
Takahashi seasonal air-sea flux climatology). Do NOT start there.

